{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSNbUTbqY9cEHmZYvJEe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw `ConflictException` with error codes for 409 responses\n- Controllers throw `ResourceNotFoundException` with error codes for 404 responses\n- GlobalExceptionHandler catches all ApiExceptions and formats them via ApiError envelope\n- Error codes are centrally defined in ErrorCode enum\n- Tests use MockMvc with status matchers and jsonPath assertions\n- POST endpoints return ResponseEntity with appropriate status\n\n**Affected files:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt`: Add the `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method\n- `ApiError.kt`: Add error code for invalid shipment state (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt`: Add tests for confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Need to define appropriate error code for CANCELLED state rejection\n- Idempotency must work correctly for already-CONFIRMED shipments\n- Must not break existing tests\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What error code name for rejecting CANCELLED confirmation? Looking at pattern (ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS), I'll use SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE to indicate the shipment cannot transition to CONFIRMED from its current state.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is already CONFIRMED or when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment (both cases are invalid state transitions).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Fetches the shipment by ID, throwing ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and returns the updated shipment\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns the shipment unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four tests:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error code\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n- Adding a service layer: The existing pattern in this codebase is thin controllers directly using repositories. Adding a service would be unrelated refactoring outside scope.\n- Using different error codes for CONFIRMED vs CANCELLED cases: The ticket specifies both should return 409, and semantically both represent invalid state transitions, so one code is appropriate.\n- Making confirm idempotent only for CONFIRMED, failing on CANCELLED: The ticket explicitly requires retry success, and idempotence is standard REST practice for state transitions.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Returns | Status | Via |\n|------|------|-------|---------|--------|-----|\n| Create CREATED → CONFIRMED | Shipment by ID | Updated shipment in repo | Shipment object | 200 | ResponseEntity.ok() |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED (idempotent) | Shipment by ID | Nothing | Shipment object | 200 | ResponseEntity.ok() |\n| Confirm CANCELLED (invalid) | Shipment by ID | Nothing | ApiError with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE | 409 | ConflictException handler |\n| Confirm non-existent | Nothing | Nothing | ApiError with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 | ResourceNotFoundException handler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirms a created shipment transitions to confirmed` - Verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and returned status\n2. `confirms an already confirmed shipment succeeds without change` - Verifies idempotency with 200 response\n3. `rejects confirmation of a cancelled shipment with conflict` - Verifies 409 for CANCELLED state\n4. `rejects confirmation of unknown shipment as not found` - Verifies 404 for missing shipment\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":20006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3f2bc9a-5da4-400e-8f5b-cfe116ab4fb1","uuid":"b62115de-b7f4-4dbc-8265-4dc955f6f35b","timestamp":"2026-09-26T16:33:39.284Z","request_id":"req_011CfSNbU538NSAaVg7CWDY9"}
